1
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:11,080
And try stepping back, would you?

2
00:00:20,080 --> 00:00:24,240
Anyone without money, come to my place.

3
00:00:24,240 --> 00:00:28,940
I don't have any either, so don't worry.

4
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:32,760
Look at the blue sky.

5
00:00:33,640 --> 00:00:35,980
White clouds.

6
00:01:05,980 --> 00:01:07,720
Tokomachi gets the ball in!

7
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:13,720
8. Certainly.

8
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:21,880
We'll contact you as soon as it's in stock.
Getting the latest plasma TV

9
00:01:21,880 --> 00:01:27,080
this cheaply almost feels unfair to the neighbors.
You're lucky, sir.

10
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,780
All you have to do is run in
the sports day and win the prize.

11
00:01:33,780 --> 00:01:36,420
This 100,000 yen is all mine.

12
00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:37,760
Easy win.

13
00:01:39,120 --> 00:01:41,360
A police station sports day?

14
00:01:41,700 --> 00:01:43,200
The prizes are amazing.

15
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:45,840
They've got designer goods
and even overseas trips.

16
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:47,340
Wow.

17
00:01:47,340 --> 00:01:49,860
Ooh, that's amazing!

18
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:51,860
Hey, why don't we all enter?

19
00:01:52,180 --> 00:01:53,560
Like a four-person relay or something.

20
00:01:54,120 --> 00:01:54,840
Komachi.

21
00:01:55,340 --> 00:01:58,520
I'm definitely taking that Gaultier watch.

22
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:03,760
I've already chosen my events,
so find someone else for the relay.

23
00:02:06,320 --> 00:02:10,520
What do you mean you
can't compete now, Maria?

24
00:02:10,520 --> 00:02:12,620
I'm sorry, Ryo-sama.

25
00:02:12,620 --> 00:02:18,200
But apparently the three-legged race
requires a male-female pair to enter.

26
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:20,900
Even though I'm a woman at heart,

27
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:23,880
my body is male, so it's not allowed.

28
00:02:26,300 --> 00:02:29,980
We even practiced, and now,
after all this, such a thing...

29
00:02:31,180 --> 00:02:32,980
Ryo-chan, what's wrong?

30
00:02:33,900 --> 00:02:37,080
Reiko, a woman in both
heart and body, Reiko.

31
00:02:37,080 --> 00:02:39,660
Please join me in the three-legged race.

32
00:02:39,660 --> 00:02:41,820
And help me win first place.

33
00:02:43,820 --> 00:02:46,740
Please, join me in the three-legged race.

34
00:02:47,880 --> 00:02:50,680
But why the three-legged race, senpai?

35
00:02:52,040 --> 00:02:53,200
Because it's a hidden
gem with less competition.

36
00:02:55,840 --> 00:03:01,180
For the sprint, every police station will surely send in young runners,
fighting for their prestige.

37
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:06,020
For highly game-like events such as the
obstacle race and the object-fetching race,

38
00:03:06,020 --> 00:03:10,840
there's a good chance dark horses like police
dogs and riot squads will come out of nowhere.

39
00:03:12,040 --> 00:03:13,600
Yes, I'll do the object-fetching race.

40
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:18,520
But people want to join the three-legged race
just to look like they took part in the sports day.

41
00:03:18,520 --> 00:03:21,180
So there should be many who
sign up for it carelessly.

42
00:03:21,180 --> 00:03:26,540
Plus, once two grown adults tie their legs together,
their fighting spirit should wilt.

43
00:03:27,160 --> 00:03:30,980
On top of that, if it's a male-female pair,
folk dancing is a given too.

44
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:35,940
If we go in there with real determination,
we should win easily.

45
00:03:36,580 --> 00:03:40,260
Sorry, but I'm already
registered for the women's relay.

46
00:03:42,220 --> 00:03:44,120
Already registered? What's that?

47
00:03:44,700 --> 00:03:48,200
Don't tell me, Senpai,
you still haven't registered?

48
00:03:48,740 --> 00:03:51,060
You can't take part in the
sports day unless you register.

49
00:03:51,900 --> 00:03:55,460
The registration deadline is 5 p.m. today,
I think.

50
00:04:05,240 --> 00:04:09,540
Well then, registration for
the sports day is now closed.

51
00:04:09,540 --> 00:04:10,280
Wait!

52
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:13,500
I'm signing up for the
three-legged race too.

53
00:04:13,500 --> 00:04:15,880
I'll definitely find a
partner by the day of the event.

54
00:04:16,700 --> 00:04:21,640
Since more people want to join the three-legged race than there are spots,
we'll hold a lottery.

55
00:04:21,640 --> 00:04:23,120
Lottery.

56
00:04:30,860 --> 00:04:34,580
Why are there so many people
wanting to do the three-legged race?

57
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:36,500
Because it's a hidden gem.

58
00:04:38,340 --> 00:04:40,700
Guess everyone's thinking the same thing.

59
00:04:40,700 --> 00:04:44,860
And it's too late now to
switch to another event.

60
00:04:46,640 --> 00:04:52,000
Since many people want to join, we've decided to
choose partners by lottery to keep things fair.

61
00:04:54,540 --> 00:05:00,180
Those who draw lots of the same color will be partners for the three-legged race,
so please don't make any mistakes.

62
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:03,260
That saves us the trouble
of finding a partner, but...

63
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:04,560
What?

64
00:05:05,640 --> 00:05:09,060
The first two people won,
so there are only two pairs left.

65
00:05:09,060 --> 00:05:11,540
If you don't draw a winning lot,
you never had a chance to begin with.

66
00:05:12,580 --> 00:05:13,480
Ready... go!

67
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:14,440
Yes!

68
00:05:14,500 --> 00:05:16,140
Here we go! Another winner!

69
00:05:16,300 --> 00:05:17,620
There's only one pair left!

70
00:05:18,020 --> 00:05:19,080
Hold on a second!

71
00:05:28,460 --> 00:05:29,480
Loon...

72
00:05:29,480 --> 00:05:32,620
Mm. Mm.

73
00:05:33,460 --> 00:05:35,080
Mm. Mm.

74
00:05:35,080 --> 00:05:36,120
Mm. Mm.

75
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:44,340
Yay, I won!

76
00:05:48,860 --> 00:05:51,620
Komachi, don't tell me you're...

77
00:05:56,260 --> 00:06:02,200
There's no way I can do a three-legged race with this cockroach-like, perverted gorilla caveman!
Absolutely not!

78
00:06:02,200 --> 00:06:07,160
Same here! I'm not running with some loud-mouthed,
bratty girl who looks like she wants to be killed!

79
00:06:07,160 --> 00:06:09,860
You said that?
You filthy, disgusting monster!

80
00:06:09,860 --> 00:06:12,020
I said it, so what? Hmph.

81
00:06:12,820 --> 00:06:14,700
Well then, since you two are dangerous,

82
00:06:15,360 --> 00:06:18,060
we're asking you to change
to different partners.

83
00:06:18,060 --> 00:06:22,020
That's right. Right now, there's nothing wrong with
swapping with someone from another pair, is there?

84
00:06:22,700 --> 00:06:27,000
It's the rule. You either pair up as two people or withdraw from the event.
Those are your only options.

85
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:31,780
Stop it, stop it, stop it!

86
00:06:32,300 --> 00:06:40,520
Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop!

87
00:06:41,680 --> 00:06:46,500
To get that Gaultier watch, it might
be better to team up with the savage.

88
00:06:46,920 --> 00:06:51,920
Since I can't pair with Maria or Reiko, maybe partnering
with the wild child Komachi is the shortest route.

89
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:54,400
Alright!

90
00:06:55,800 --> 00:06:59,640
Komachi! The truce only lasts
until the day of the sports day!

91
00:07:00,080 --> 00:07:00,780
Fine.

92
00:07:02,200 --> 00:07:05,560
Then the three pairs for the
three-legged race have been decided.

93
00:07:06,520 --> 00:07:08,160
Aaaaaah!

94
00:07:08,160 --> 00:07:12,820
Alright. Since it's settled, there's no time to waste.
Let's get started right away.

95
00:07:12,820 --> 00:07:16,300
Isn't that Komachi?

96
00:07:18,280 --> 00:07:21,980
Mom, how's it going?
Are you all set for the Taiwan trip?

97
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:25,900
Yes, your father and
I are packing right now.

98
00:07:26,260 --> 00:07:31,140
Since we're going all the way to Tokyo, your
father says he wants to see Komachi's face.

99
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:36,880
Sorry, I have something on Sunday that I simply can't get out of,
so I can't come to see you off.

100
00:07:37,520 --> 00:07:39,340
Komachi says she has
something to take care of.

101
00:07:40,700 --> 00:07:42,360
Komachi, it's Dad.

102
00:07:42,360 --> 00:07:46,020
Have fun on your trip with Mom, Dad.

103
00:07:46,440 --> 00:07:51,300
It's Komachi's silver wedding anniversary gift,
so we'll enjoy it together.

104
00:07:51,840 --> 00:07:54,080
Dad, why don't you ask about that too?

105
00:07:54,080 --> 00:07:58,880
Komachi,
how are things between you and Ryotsu now?

106
00:07:58,880 --> 00:08:01,440
Ryotsu Kankichi-san.

107
00:08:01,840 --> 00:08:03,900
The one with thick eyebrows and short legs.

108
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:06,800
Look, you two are still saying that?

109
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:09,720
That I could ever end up
with a barbarian like him?

110
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:11,240
How many times do I have to say it?

111
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:13,920
There you are, Komachi.
I've been looking for you.

112
00:08:13,920 --> 00:08:16,220
I'm on the phone, so don't talk to me.

113
00:08:16,740 --> 00:08:18,300
That was Ryotsu's voice just now, wasn't it?

114
00:08:18,300 --> 00:08:20,800
So it wasn't over after all.

115
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:22,280
That's good news, Dad.

116
00:08:22,280 --> 00:08:23,900
I'm relieved, Komachi.

117
00:08:24,360 --> 00:08:26,820
I won't interfere,
so you two work things out together.

118
00:08:26,820 --> 00:08:27,600
Well then, bye.

119
00:08:29,140 --> 00:08:29,860
Whoa -

120
00:08:30,380 --> 00:08:32,360
She's lost it!

121
00:08:32,780 --> 00:08:34,520
Are these country mothers?

122
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:38,420
Look what you did!
Now they've got the wrong idea again.

123
00:08:38,900 --> 00:08:42,380
You don't think Komachi and I are,
like, actually together, do you?

124
00:08:43,060 --> 00:08:46,080
No matter how many times I explain,
the misunderstanding just keeps growing.

125
00:08:46,900 --> 00:08:47,680
What's your problem?

126
00:08:48,460 --> 00:08:51,900
Before the sports day,
practice the three-legged race with me.

127
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:54,540
Practice? You've got to be joking.

128
00:08:54,540 --> 00:08:56,020
You perverted pig.

129
00:08:56,020 --> 00:08:59,220
I've got a group mixer with
a bunch of handsome guys today.

130
00:08:59,220 --> 00:09:03,140
One three-legged race with you
on the day is more than enough.

131
00:09:03,140 --> 00:09:06,000
If you want to practice so badly,
go do it with a mannequin.

132
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:07,360
See ya!

133
00:09:11,420 --> 00:09:12,540
Damn it! Dammit!

134
00:09:32,140 --> 00:09:33,580
That hurts already!

135
00:09:33,580 --> 00:09:37,100
Bear with it! If it comes untied halfway,
we're disqualified.

136
00:09:39,140 --> 00:09:39,540
Okay.

137
00:09:41,420 --> 00:09:46,740
Fine, but if we don't stick together, how are we supposed to run?
I'm not interested in a girl like you!

138
00:09:46,740 --> 00:09:52,680
What did you say? Well,
just get in position already, we're going!

139
00:09:52,680 --> 00:09:56,740
I get it, you don't have to keep telling me!
Get set...

140
00:09:59,960 --> 00:10:04,840
Hey, what are you doing?
I told you to start with the right foot!

141
00:10:04,840 --> 00:10:06,600
No, start with the left!

142
00:10:06,720 --> 00:10:07,820
Your right!

143
00:10:08,060 --> 00:10:10,440
I thought you meant your right foot!

144
00:10:10,620 --> 00:10:12,320
Don't say such confusing things!

145
00:10:13,240 --> 00:10:14,520
Show some consideration for others!

146
00:10:15,260 --> 00:10:15,920
Hey!

147
00:10:17,760 --> 00:10:19,580
Because of you, we got off to a slow start!

148
00:10:20,100 --> 00:10:21,080
So it's my fault now?!

149
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:23,400
This time we start with the inside foot!

150
00:10:23,640 --> 00:10:24,520
Ready, go!

151
00:10:25,100 --> 00:10:25,640
Go!

152
00:10:26,220 --> 00:10:27,340
Gar Clutch!

153
00:10:27,640 --> 00:10:27,800
Gar Clutch!

154
00:10:28,620 --> 00:10:30,020
The Gardier watch!

155
00:10:32,140 --> 00:10:33,660
Plasma TV!

156
00:11:04,980 --> 00:11:07,547
Tako, that was just the qualifier.
We came second, so

157
00:11:07,597 --> 00:11:09,940
all we have to do is win the final,
you fool!

158
00:11:17,300 --> 00:11:18,820
There you are, Komachi.

159
00:11:19,520 --> 00:11:22,384
What? The final's still an hour away,

160
00:11:22,434 --> 00:11:24,620
so what I do until then
is my business, right?

161
00:11:26,100 --> 00:11:28,334
I checked out the lineup for the final,

162
00:11:28,384 --> 00:11:30,400
and it won't be like the qualifier.

163
00:11:30,660 --> 00:11:31,960
They look strong?

164
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:32,080
What do you think?

165
00:11:32,980 --> 00:11:36,718
If we run out of sync like we just did,

166
00:11:36,768 --> 00:11:40,400
we'll never beat them.
We won't get the TV or the watch!

167
00:11:40,820 --> 00:11:44,320
But there's no way I can
match my steps with yours.

168
00:11:45,260 --> 00:11:48,980
The secret weapon that makes
the impossible possible is this.

169
00:11:57,100 --> 00:11:58,720
W-what is this?!

170
00:11:59,200 --> 00:12:04,960
It's the three-legged race victory machine I stayed up all night building yesterday,
Issin Dōtai-kun!

171
00:12:04,960 --> 00:12:06,740
"Issin Dōtai-kun"?

172
00:12:06,740 --> 00:12:08,020
Come on, come on.

173
00:12:09,100 --> 00:12:15,380
If Komachi and I drill the three-legged race into our bodies with this for a full hour,
we're guaranteed to win.

174
00:12:15,380 --> 00:12:16,940
Guaranteed?

175
00:12:18,040 --> 00:12:19,240
Victory is certain.

176
00:12:23,040 --> 00:12:23,480
Yes.

177
00:12:24,540 --> 00:12:27,400
Mom, you've already arrived at the airport?

178
00:12:28,980 --> 00:12:30,940
What? Why are you there?

179
00:12:30,940 --> 00:12:34,940
Dad pretended to know the way and kept saying,
"This way, this way!"

180
00:12:34,940 --> 00:12:36,920
It all started with Mom,

181
00:12:36,920 --> 00:12:40,260
but today I've finally had it with Dad.

182
00:12:40,260 --> 00:12:42,460
Dad, I've reached my limit too.

183
00:12:42,460 --> 00:12:44,480
Yes, that's why, Komachi.

184
00:12:44,480 --> 00:12:47,480
Don't fight over such silly things.
Right now, it's still

185
00:12:50,920 --> 00:12:51,940
I snapped.

186
00:12:52,540 --> 00:12:53,880
What on earth is going on?

187
00:12:53,880 --> 00:12:58,220
Today my parents won a
Taiwan trip in a bank raffle.

188
00:12:58,720 --> 00:13:01,113
And yet, instead of Haneda,
where the airport is,

189
00:13:01,163 --> 00:13:03,200
they're apparently in Akabane right now!

190
00:13:07,380 --> 00:13:09,680
All you're doing is the
"feather" character, you know!

191
00:13:11,220 --> 00:13:12,746
That's the kind of couple they are.

192
00:13:12,796 --> 00:13:16,580
On top of that, they're nervous from
traveling abroad when they're not used to it.

193
00:13:17,720 --> 00:13:20,520
I should've gone to pick them
up at Tokyo Station after all.

194
00:13:21,380 --> 00:13:22,500
I'm going to go over there for a bit.

195
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:23,320
Whoa!

196
00:13:23,480 --> 00:13:24,300
Whoa!

197
00:13:24,840 --> 00:13:26,060
Go where?

198
00:13:26,060 --> 00:13:28,440
I'm taking the two of them to Haneda.

199
00:13:28,440 --> 00:13:30,000
Hurry up and take this weird thing off.

200
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:32,200
What about the final?

201
00:13:34,380 --> 00:13:34,780
Hey,

202
00:13:35,360 --> 00:13:36,580
hello, it's me.

203
00:13:36,580 --> 00:13:37,540
It's Ryotsu.

204
00:13:38,020 --> 00:13:39,120
Ryotsu-san.

205
00:13:39,120 --> 00:13:41,120
We married folks are hopeless.

206
00:13:41,120 --> 00:13:43,240
Please look after our Komachi.

207
00:13:43,240 --> 00:13:45,260
No, that's not what I meant.

208
00:13:45,260 --> 00:13:47,120
Komachi's right now I'm

209
00:13:47,120 --> 00:13:49,080
no, I can't let go of my feet,

210
00:13:49,080 --> 00:13:50,760
ask at the nearest police box.

211
00:13:50,760 --> 00:13:52,600
Hurry over to Haneda right away!

212
00:13:52,600 --> 00:13:53,480
Is that Ryotsu?

213
00:13:53,480 --> 00:13:57,740
I can't believe I've put up with
a wife like this for 25 years.

214
00:13:57,740 --> 00:14:00,000
Husbands and wives are strangers after all.

215
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:04,520
Ryotsu, if you're planning to be with Komachi too,
think about that carefully, okay?

216
00:14:04,900 --> 00:14:06,660
No, I have no such intention at all.

217
00:14:06,660 --> 00:14:09,120
That's how it is, Ryotsu.

218
00:14:09,120 --> 00:14:10,760
What do you mean, "that's how it is"?

219
00:14:11,380 --> 00:14:15,540
Looks like the time has come for
us to start walking separate paths.

220
00:14:15,540 --> 00:14:16,460
...or something.

221
00:14:16,460 --> 00:14:18,860
Walking separate paths

222
00:14:18,860 --> 00:14:23,240
What? Just because Dad and Mom got lost,
what are you going on about?

223
00:14:23,480 --> 00:14:26,080
Listen! Head to Hamamatsucho right now!

224
00:14:26,160 --> 00:14:28,000
If you go to Hamamatsu, you'd better not!
I mean it!

225
00:14:32,840 --> 00:14:34,580
Take this off right now!

226
00:14:34,880 --> 00:14:36,460
Oh no, I left the key in the room!

227
00:14:36,700 --> 00:14:38,940
That's why we're bound together,
and this won't come off!

228
00:14:39,340 --> 00:14:40,400
What are we going to do?!

229
00:14:40,560 --> 00:14:42,900
How am I supposed to go pick
them up with this stuck on?

230
00:14:44,220 --> 00:14:45,403
It's our silver wedding anniversary,

231
00:14:45,453 --> 00:14:48,800
and you get lost in Akabane,
and now our divorce is on the line?

232
00:14:49,180 --> 00:14:50,500
That's just not fair!

233
00:14:53,440 --> 00:14:57,060
If it's come to this, I'll go with you too.
You've got to be joking.

234
00:14:57,780 --> 00:15:05,960
I can't compete in the finals alone, so the
safest way is to go together and hurry back.

235
00:15:05,960 --> 00:15:08,220
Go together,
in the two-person three-legged race?

236
00:15:08,880 --> 00:15:09,260
Do we really have to?

237
00:15:10,060 --> 00:15:10,820
Let's go!

238
00:15:16,040 --> 00:15:18,720
I'm Ono, joining today's Taiwan tour.

239
00:15:18,720 --> 00:15:19,760
Ono.

240
00:15:19,760 --> 00:15:21,780
Shojiro Ono and Masako Ono.

241
00:15:21,780 --> 00:15:24,160
I'm their daughter.

242
00:15:24,160 --> 00:15:25,200
Ours is crowded

243
00:15:25,200 --> 00:15:26,620
The train's better.

244
00:15:27,060 --> 00:15:30,320
I'll definitely be there,
so please wait for me!

245
00:15:31,260 --> 00:15:31,900
Hah.

246
00:15:31,900 --> 00:15:34,900
It's a red light!

247
00:15:34,900 --> 00:15:38,440
Once we're one body running through the sky,
we can't stop easily.

248
00:15:40,980 --> 00:15:42,940
Can't we even stomp in place with this?

249
00:15:42,940 --> 00:15:45,500
It has no play, just like a keirin pedal.

250
00:15:45,500 --> 00:15:47,020
It all comes down to giving
it everything we've got.

251
00:15:48,240 --> 00:15:51,180
Just, just, just, just, just,
just, just, just, just, just...

252
00:15:54,460 --> 00:15:55,840
Whoa, we're gonna hit something!

253
00:15:55,840 --> 00:15:56,800
Turn!

254
00:15:58,940 --> 00:16:00,460
This is a stupid gag.

255
00:16:01,160 --> 00:16:03,340
We can't stop,
but we can go backwards, right?

256
00:16:07,940 --> 00:16:10,880
We have to change direction somewhere,
or it'll be hard to run like this.

257
00:16:11,260 --> 00:16:14,340
To change direction,
we've gotta crash into something again.

258
00:16:14,340 --> 00:16:19,640
We changed direction nicely.

259
00:16:19,640 --> 00:16:21,160
Not nicely at all!

260
00:16:21,160 --> 00:16:22,300
Watch out!

261
00:16:25,040 --> 00:16:26,740
Tell me sooner!

262
00:16:26,740 --> 00:16:28,420
Next up, the footbridge!

263
00:16:28,420 --> 00:16:28,720
What?

264
00:16:31,660 --> 00:16:33,040
Going uphill is still fine.

265
00:16:33,340 --> 00:16:35,240
The real problem is going downhill!

266
00:16:47,860 --> 00:16:51,340
Next is the top... the top...

267
00:17:01,560 --> 00:17:03,060
Dad, Dad.

268
00:17:05,780 --> 00:17:07,760
Dad, Dad.

269
00:17:07,760 --> 00:17:15,320
As expected of you, Nakagawa. Congratulations
on finishing first in the qualifiers.

270
00:17:15,320 --> 00:17:19,120
You were the one who came first in the scavenger race,
Terai-san, weren't you?

271
00:17:20,440 --> 00:17:21,740
Kei-chan, Terai-san.

272
00:17:22,180 --> 00:17:25,580
Reiko-san, everyone, good luck in the relay!

273
00:17:26,180 --> 00:17:27,380
My heart's pounding!

274
00:17:27,840 --> 00:17:31,900
I can't see Komachi-chan and Ryo-chan's
three-legged race pair anywhere.

275
00:17:32,540 --> 00:17:34,800
We've been looking for them too, but...

276
00:17:35,600 --> 00:17:38,200
I wonder if they're secretly
practicing somewhere.

277
00:17:39,380 --> 00:17:41,840
It's all because you made this weird thing.

278
00:17:42,220 --> 00:17:44,720
I'm the one who's been dragged
around and is suffering because of it!

279
00:17:45,220 --> 00:17:46,460
It can't be helped.

280
00:17:47,200 --> 00:17:50,800
I didn't expect things to
turn out like this either!

281
00:17:51,980 --> 00:17:54,440
Can't you get in touch
with Mom and the others?

282
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:56,920
They don't have cell phones, you know.

283
00:17:56,920 --> 00:17:59,900
We have no choice but to
wait for them to contact us.

284
00:18:01,040 --> 00:18:02,320
Hello, Dad?

285
00:18:03,400 --> 00:18:04,540
What, they got separated?

286
00:18:05,660 --> 00:18:06,520
Sa-a-at.

287
00:18:07,100 --> 00:18:09,560
Dad and Mom got lost, they said.

288
00:18:09,560 --> 00:18:10,400
What?

289
00:18:11,540 --> 00:18:12,200
Hello?

290
00:18:12,200 --> 00:18:15,820
Never mind, Dad, just take the
next train and chase after Mom.

291
00:18:16,580 --> 00:18:18,460
Not Hamamatsu, Hamamatsucho.

292
00:18:18,460 --> 00:18:20,500
We're heading there now too.

293
00:18:21,480 --> 00:18:23,520
I wonder what Mom's doing.

294
00:18:25,040 --> 00:18:27,120
Yes, Mom? It's me, Ryotsu.

295
00:18:27,120 --> 00:18:30,520
OK, it's fine. Mom, just go on ahead.

296
00:18:30,920 --> 00:18:32,380
Did you get off?

297
00:18:32,580 --> 00:18:34,440
Did you get off the train at Okachimachi?

298
00:18:34,920 --> 00:18:37,360
Because you don't have a cell phone.

299
00:18:37,360 --> 00:18:41,000
I got off the train and I'm
calling from a payphone, Mom.

300
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:41,940
Get on, get on!

301
00:18:41,940 --> 00:18:44,820
Take the next train and don't
get off until Hamamatsucho.

302
00:18:48,340 --> 00:18:50,260
That's just the kind of couple they are.

303
00:19:01,040 --> 00:19:02,200
Masako

304
00:19:02,200 --> 00:19:03,880
Masako

305
00:19:03,880 --> 00:19:04,600
Masako

306
00:19:05,440 --> 00:19:06,400
Dad

307
00:19:07,120 --> 00:19:08,080
Thank goodness.

308
00:19:09,280 --> 00:19:11,640
Please don't stop near the entrance.

309
00:19:12,840 --> 00:19:13,320
Ugh.

310
00:19:13,320 --> 00:19:14,580
You're such a klutz.

311
00:19:16,460 --> 00:19:18,100
The doors are closing. Please be careful.

312
00:19:25,580 --> 00:19:26,360
Reiko!

313
00:19:27,100 --> 00:19:27,420
Yes!

314
00:19:30,780 --> 00:19:32,660
Reiko! Hang in there!

315
00:19:33,520 --> 00:19:34,800
I can see the station, Komachi!

316
00:19:35,460 --> 00:19:36,340
Yay!

317
00:19:36,520 --> 00:19:38,960
Okuno-san's train is about to crash in too!

318
00:19:40,600 --> 00:19:41,820
Hello, Mom?

319
00:19:42,800 --> 00:19:45,000
Uossho! Uossho!

320
00:19:46,460 --> 00:19:49,400
Where are you right now?
Everyone's looking for you.

321
00:19:53,120 --> 00:19:55,600
Komachi, looks like she's on the phone.

322
00:19:58,160 --> 00:19:59,900
Yeah, yeah, excuse me for a second.

323
00:19:59,900 --> 00:20:01,413
Sorry, sorry,

324
00:20:01,463 --> 00:20:03,920
I'll explain the details later.

325
00:20:06,680 --> 00:20:09,640
Where are you? Shojiro Ono and Masako Ono!

326
00:20:09,640 --> 00:20:10,620
Komachi!

327
00:20:10,620 --> 00:20:12,780
Ryo-san, we're over here, over here!

328
00:20:13,380 --> 00:20:14,900
Dad, Mom!

329
00:20:16,460 --> 00:20:16,780
Later!

330
00:20:35,220 --> 00:20:37,460
So we're stuck like this
until we reach the airport?!

331
00:20:40,020 --> 00:20:42,703
Honestly, Dad and Mom,

332
00:20:42,753 --> 00:20:44,480
you two are a real headache!

333
00:20:46,460 --> 00:20:49,100
At least I got to see Komachi's face before the start,
so whatever.

334
00:20:49,100 --> 00:20:51,440
All's well that ends well, right?

335
00:20:51,440 --> 00:20:53,220
It's not over yet, you know.

336
00:20:53,700 --> 00:20:56,300
Hello, yes,
this is Ono from the Taiwan tour.

337
00:20:57,180 --> 00:21:00,980
S-sorry, we're arriving shortly,
almost there.

338
00:21:00,980 --> 00:21:05,180
Looking at them again,
they really are a perfectly matched couple.

339
00:21:05,680 --> 00:21:06,620
They really are.

340
00:21:07,400 --> 00:21:11,120
After we get back from the trip, we'll go
properly to Ryo-chan's parents to greet them.

341
00:21:11,120 --> 00:21:12,340
No need to go, really.

342
00:21:13,140 --> 00:21:15,800
I've reached my limit.

343
00:21:18,040 --> 00:21:21,640
Mr. Ono? Over here, over here!

344
00:21:24,880 --> 00:21:26,400
Nice to meet you.

345
00:21:26,400 --> 00:21:28,040
I'm off.

346
00:21:28,040 --> 00:21:30,880
Those are my daughter and cat.

347
00:21:30,880 --> 00:21:32,540
Made it in time.

348
00:21:32,540 --> 00:21:34,420
Sports day.

349
00:21:38,700 --> 00:21:40,420
Next up,

350
00:21:42,980 --> 00:21:45,480
Lane 1, Shinjuku Prize team.

351
00:21:45,480 --> 00:21:48,440
Lane 2, Arakawa Prize team.

352
00:21:48,900 --> 00:21:51,640
Lane 3, Setagaya Prize team.

353
00:21:51,640 --> 00:21:54,720
Lane 4, Suginami Prize team.

354
00:21:55,140 --> 00:21:57,600
Lane 5, Katsushika Prize team.

355
00:21:57,600 --> 00:22:00,560
Is the Lane 5,
Katsushika Prize team dangerous?

356
00:22:04,400 --> 00:22:06,720
What happened to them?
Ryo-chan and the others?

357
00:22:06,720 --> 00:22:09,400
Senpai, they were so eager to compete.

358
00:22:09,400 --> 00:22:10,580
Here they come!

359
00:22:12,340 --> 00:22:14,860
Ready

360
00:22:14,860 --> 00:22:15,660
Get set!

361
00:22:15,660 --> 00:22:16,000
Mm.

362
00:22:20,060 --> 00:22:25,680
They made it in time,
but still, at this rate...

363
00:22:26,350 --> 00:22:28,000
After coming all this way...

364
00:22:30,410 --> 00:22:33,960
My legs feel light. This could work out.

365
00:22:33,960 --> 00:22:35,220
Aaaaaah!

366
00:22:48,760 --> 00:22:49,460
Yes!

367
00:22:49,620 --> 00:22:50,100
We did it!

368
00:22:50,100 --> 00:22:51,720
Chief, Ryotsu did it!

369
00:22:51,720 --> 00:22:53,980
Good for you, Ohara-kun.

370
00:22:54,540 --> 00:22:55,940
We did it! We won!

371
00:22:56,100 --> 00:22:58,500
Ryotsu's team won the championship too!

372
00:22:58,700 --> 00:23:00,080
We did it! We won!

373
00:23:00,280 --> 00:23:01,600
A plasma TV!

374
00:23:02,040 --> 00:23:02,760
Yes!

375
00:23:05,220 --> 00:23:07,440
Lane five, Katsushika Police Station team,
disqualified!

376
00:23:07,840 --> 00:23:09,320
What? Why?

377
00:23:09,800 --> 00:23:12,300
Your legs weren't tied,
so you're disqualified!

378
00:23:12,560 --> 00:23:15,740
No way!

379
00:23:19,720 --> 00:23:20,750
Ryo-san,

380
00:23:20,800 --> 00:23:24,580
what happened to that plasma TV business?

381
00:23:24,680 --> 00:23:27,340
I-I'm building it right now.

382
00:23:27,800 --> 00:23:31,420
It's not a plastic model kit,
so even you can't build it, Ryo-san.

383
00:23:31,420 --> 00:23:32,760
Ryo, I need a time base!

384
00:23:32,760 --> 00:23:58,200
!

385
00:23:58,200 --> 00:23:59,600
Maybe,

386
00:23:59,600 --> 00:24:00,900
it might just happen.

387
00:24:01,560 --> 00:24:02,960
Absolutely not.

388
00:24:28,200 --> 00:24:29,920
Why is that, I wonder?

389
00:24:31,940 --> 00:24:43,400
Why does someone's personality change when they ride a motorbike, I wonder?
Why do the cicadas, once fairies, only wake once every four years?

390
00:24:43,400 --> 00:24:49,080
I wonder why.
Nakagawa is a mass-produced model.

391
00:24:49,080 --> 00:24:52,560
He won't lend money, though,

392
00:24:52,560 --> 00:24:56,340
but he lends out tanks
and fighter jets so easily.

393
00:24:56,340 --> 00:24:59,940
I wonder why.

394
00:25:02,220 --> 00:25:07,020
Reiko is incredibly rich, though,

395
00:25:08,660 --> 00:25:10,760
yet she works at the police box.

396
00:25:10,760 --> 00:25:12,500
I wonder why.

397
00:25:13,400 --> 00:25:14,760
I wonder why.

398
00:25:14,760 --> 00:25:16,040
Why is that?

399
00:25:16,040 --> 00:25:17,960
Why, why, why?

400
00:25:30,060 --> 00:25:33,180
Damn it, no matter how many times we try,
it's the worst day ever.

401
00:25:33,180 --> 00:25:35,500
This fortune-telling where you pick A or B,

402
00:25:35,500 --> 00:25:39,120
no matter which way we go, we always end up right here.
What on earth is going on?

403
00:25:39,580 --> 00:25:40,620
What's this incident?

404
00:25:40,620 --> 00:25:44,040
On a day like this, I've got a bad feeling.

405
00:25:44,460 --> 00:25:47,480
See you next time at the fateful crossroads.

406
00:25:50,080 --> 00:25:51,700
Kameari-ri!

407
00:25:51,700 --> 00:25:54,260
Surely it's Kameari-ri!

408
00:25:54,820 --> 00:25:59,240
Everybody, come on over to our town!

409
00:26:00,060 --> 00:26:00,820
Thank you!

